WEBVTT

NOTE Build the approach graph. English captions.

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.673
Start with y equals negative
three-fourths x plus six.

2
00:00:05.323 --> 00:00:11.644
When x is zero, y is six, so
plot the y-intercept, zero, six.

3
00:00:12.294 --> 00:00:15.927
The slope means right four
seconds and down three meters.

4
00:00:16.677 --> 00:00:18.359
Plot four, three.

5
00:00:21.309 --> 00:00:26.130
Repeat the same changes to reach
eight, zero, the x-intercept.

6
00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:29.676
Zero distance remaining means arrival.

7
00:00:30.426 --> 00:00:34.519
Connect the points with a straight
segment from zero through eight seconds.

8
00:00:35.269 --> 00:00:37.790
This graph shows distance
remaining over time;

9
00:00:37.790 --> 00:00:40.572
it does not show a
downward physical route.
